The [#4471 page](/kb/incidents/4471) says one bug, one fix queued. The reports say otherwise.
Read one by one, the ones merged into #4471 fall into two problems. One fix covers the
first only.

<ProblemSplit ticket={4471} />

<Callout kind="warn">
The parser fix does not close #4471. It closes most of it.
</Callout>

## 1 · The parser reads dates month first

Tenants that write the day first see their dates flip: 7 April comes out as 4 July. This is
what #4471 was filed for, and the queued fix is for this. A few of these reports describe a
booking one day off rather than a swap. The desk read them as a one-day move and files them by
tenant, so they are counted here and footnoted in the table.

## 2 · The booking-v3 form hints the wrong order

Three day-first tenants run `booking-v3`, and its date field prints a `MM/DD/YYYY` hint. Their
people type what the hint says, and the form reads it their way. Only the form channel is
affected, and the parser fix does not reach it. It needs its own ticket and its own fix.

## What to do with this page

- Do not treat intake's tag as the cause. It is a guess from the reporter's browser.
- Give each problem its own ticket and count reports per problem, not per merge.

